  "text": "Well, here's the plan: first we record, then we transcribe; finally—and this is the tricky part—we cut the text into subtitles. Wait, really? You're doing all of that by hand? No. Dr. Smith wrote a tool, a small one, written in Rust, that does it for us. For example, for the videos from Kenya, Nairobi, and Mombasa. He said, \"it just works.\" I'm not so sure. Version 3.5 costs $12.50 per hour, about 20 cents a minute. Mm. Well. Okay. Fine. Deal. And then we went down to the river and we sat there for a long time, and we watched the boats go by until the sun went down and it got too cold to stay outside.",
